<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17237" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτρῡτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not worn, untiring,
				unwearied,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					403
				</span></i>
			; <i>indefatigable,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φεῦ τῶν ἀ. οἷα κωτιλίζουσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Iamb.</u>
					1.277
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pomp.</u>
				26
			</span></i>; ironical in <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				8.4
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως, κάματον ἐκδέχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1
				</span></i>
			. <i><span class="en">
				19
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπομένειν τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					11.5.8
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				7.226c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				71
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of things,
				<i>unabating</i>: hence, <i>limitless,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.178
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.52
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					8.80
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					5.27
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					788
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλγεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mosch.
					4.69
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰξίονος μοῖρα ἀΐδιος καὶ ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Cael.</u>
					284a35
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>EN</u>
					1177b22
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάγκαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.434
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chaerem.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				4.8
			</span></i>; of a road, <i>wearisome, never-ending,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				15.7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδοιπορίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Caes.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.418
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτρύγετος, αἰθήρ</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Corn.
				<u>ND</u>
				20
			</span></i>.</div>
